        ],
        "raw_source_snapshot": {
          "path": "E:/Samplinglib/runs/20261007-companion-priority/pbps-real-root-unique62/next-macro-source63/primary-11-A2-SS2-p5.exactraw.snapshot.html",
          "raw_bytes": 5849,
          "lf_bytes": 5849,
          "raw_sha256": "2806c44543820aa78989755ce7b284dd2da96c38c5013d193b1d323d64ca864e",
          "lf_sha256": "2806c44543820aa78989755ce7b284dd2da96c38c5013d193b1d323d64ca864e"
        },
        "literal_text": "Since \\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}} is boundedly invertible on \\mathfrak{H}_{\\mathsf{P},0}, (B.11) gives the polar decomposition \\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}=\\mathsf{V}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}\\,,\\hskip 20.00003pt\\mathsf{V}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}\\coloneqq\\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}^{-1}\\,:\\mathfrak{H}_{\\mathsf{P},0}\\longrightarrow\\mathfrak{H}_{\\perp}\\,,\\hskip 20.00003pt\\mathsf{V}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}^{*}\\mathsf{V}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}=I_{\\mathfrak{H}_{\\mathsf{P},0}}\\,. (B.16) Here \\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}} measures the size of the microscopic component created by reflection, while the isometry \\mathsf{V}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}} records its direction in \\mathfrak{H}_{\\perp}. The next proposition says that the half-turn acts nearly as -I on the corresponding microscopic directions \\mathsf{V}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}^{-1}f.",
        "coverage": "EXCLUDED",
        "boundary": "Polar/inverse future work"
      },
