      {
        "id": "S1.p1",
        "primary": {
          "path": "E:/Samplinglib/runs/20261007-companion-priority/phase-pbps-gamma-preread57/primary-pbps.exactraw.snapshot.html",
          "raw_bytes": 1482128,
          "lf_bytes": 1482128,
          "raw_sha256": "d81e929496ff33f8895ebdb45b5b7f3eba89a069806d97d5bbbd7a6c0c032760",
          "lf_sha256": "d81e929496ff33f8895ebdb45b5b7f3eba89a069806d97d5bbbd7a6c0c032760"
        },
        "byte_range": [
          47126,
          50729
        ],
        "raw_source_snapshot": {
          "path": "E:/Samplinglib/runs/20261007-companion-priority/pbps-real-root-unique62/next-macro-source63/primary-14-S1-p1.exactraw.snapshot.html",
          "raw_bytes": 3603,
          "lf_bytes": 3603,
          "raw_sha256": "a9bc657fb926368561ab2657dfbfbf6a7a0ba5b8c2122f8d1fb8510a0a975262",
          "lf_sha256": "a9bc657fb926368561ab2657dfbfbf6a7a0ba5b8c2122f8d1fb8510a0a975262"
        },
        "literal_text": "We study the problem of sampling from the probability measure \\mu(\\mathrm{d}x)=Z^{-1}e^{-V(x)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x on \\mathbb{R}^{d}, where V\\in C^{2}(\\mathbb{R}^{d}) satisfies, for 0<\\alpha\\leq\\beta, \\alpha I\\preceq\\nabla^{2}V(x)\\preceq\\beta I\\,,\\hskip 20.00003ptx\\in\\mathbb{R}^{d}\\,,\\hskip 20.00003pt\\kappa\\coloneqq\\tfrac{\\beta}{\\alpha}\\,. (1.1) The main result of this paper is the following.",
        "coverage": "NODE_OR_CONTEXT",
        "boundary": "Bounded source prerequisite or B10/B11 statement; no wholepaper claim"
      },
      {
        "id": "S2.E6",
        "primary": {
          "path": "E:/Samplinglib/runs/20261007-companion-priority/phase-pbps-gamma-preread57/primary-pbps.exactraw.snapshot.html",
          "raw_bytes": 1482128,
          "lf_bytes": 1482128,
          "raw_sha256": "d81e929496ff33f8895ebdb45b5b7f3eba89a069806d97d5bbbd7a6c0c032760",
          "lf_sha256": "d81e929496ff33f8895ebdb45b5b7f3eba89a069806d97d5bbbd7a6c0c032760"
        },
        "byte_range": [
          96222,
