      },
      {
        "id": "A2.SS1.p1",
        "primary": {
          "path": "E:/Samplinglib/runs/20261007-companion-priority/phase-pbps-gamma-preread57/primary-pbps.exactraw.snapshot.html",
          "raw_bytes": 1482128,
          "lf_bytes": 1482128,
          "raw_sha256": "d81e929496ff33f8895ebdb45b5b7f3eba89a069806d97d5bbbd7a6c0c032760",
          "lf_sha256": "d81e929496ff33f8895ebdb45b5b7f3eba89a069806d97d5bbbd7a6c0c032760"
        },
        "byte_range": [
          708364,
          727705
        ],
        "raw_source_snapshot": {
          "path": "E:/Samplinglib/runs/20261007-companion-priority/pbps-real-root-unique62/next-macro-source63/primary-17-A2-SS1-p1.exactraw.snapshot.html",
          "raw_bytes": 19341,
          "lf_bytes": 19341,
          "raw_sha256": "395059e86bc44a9581440d09e7095e1979f6579e14a55979f5bd2fa382b6fb24",
          "lf_sha256": "395059e86bc44a9581440d09e7095e1979f6579e14a55979f5bd2fa382b6fb24"
        },
        "literal_text": "Our target distribution is the joint law \\pi_{\\eta} defined in (2.6), and we set \\mathfrak{H}\\coloneqq L^{2}(\\pi_{\\eta}). Recall from (3.11) that the ideal Proximal BPS has transition kernel \\mathcal{K}\\bigl((x,y),\\mathrm{d}x^{\\prime}\\,\\mathrm{d}y^{\\prime}\\bigr)=\\delta_{2x-y}(\\mathrm{d}y^{\\prime})\\,\\bigl[\\rho\\,\\pi_{\\eta}^{X\\mid Y=y^{\\prime}}(\\mathrm{d}x^{\\prime})+(1-\\rho)\\,\\mathcal{H}_{y^{\\prime}}(x,\\mathrm{d}x^{\\prime})\\bigr]\\,, where \\mathcal{H}_{y^{\\prime}} is the conditional half-turn kernel from Proposition 3.2. Since the algorithm is a discrete-time chain, its evolution is described by the induced one-step Markov operator on observables, (\\mathsf{K}f)(x,y)\\coloneqq\\int_{\\mathbb{R}^{2d}}f(x^{\\prime},y^{\\prime})\\,\\mathcal{K}\\bigl((x,y),\\mathrm{d}x^{\\prime}\\,\\mathrm{d}y^{\\prime}\\bigr)\\,. Thus \\mathcal{K} acts on probability laws, whereas \\mathsf{K} is its induced action on observables. The first term in brackets in \\mathcal{K} is the conditional resampling branch. After the auxiliary coordinate is updated to y^{\\prime}, this branch replaces the x-coordinate by an independent draw from \\pi_{\\eta}^{X\\mid Y=y^{\\prime}}. The associated conditional expectation operator is (\\mathsf{P}f)(x,y)\\coloneqq\\int f(x^{\\prime},y)\\,\\pi_{\\eta}^{X\\mid Y=y}(\\mathrm{d}x^{\\prime})=\\mathbb{E}[f(X,Y)\\mid Y=y]\\,. (B.1) In particular, \\mathsf{P}f depends only on the coordinate y. The range and kernel of \\mathsf{P} are \\begin{split}\\mathfrak{H}_{\\mathsf{P}}&\\coloneqq\\operatorname{ran}(\\mathsf{P})=\\{f\\in\\mathfrak{H}:f(x,y)=g(y)\\text{ for some }g\\in L^{2}(\\pi_{\\eta}^{Y})\\}\\,,\\\\ \\mathfrak{H}_{\\perp}&\\coloneqq\\ker(\\mathsf{P})=\\operatorname{ran}(\\mathsf{P}^{\\perp})=\\{f\\in\\mathfrak{H}:\\mathbb{E}[f(X,Y)\\mid Y]=0\\}\\,.\\end{split} (B.2) Here \\mathsf{P}^{\\perp}\\coloneqq I-\\mathsf{P}, so \\mathfrak{H}=\\mathfrak{H}_{\\mathsf{P}}\\oplus\\mathfrak{H}_{\\perp} and f=\\mathsf{P}f+\\mathsf{P}^{\\perp}f. In the common terminology of hypocoercivity [14, 21], \\operatorname{ran}(\\mathsf{P}) is the macroscopic subspace and its orthogonal complement is the microscopic subspace. Thus functions in \\mathfrak{H}_{\\mathsf{P}} depend only on the coordinate y, whereas functions in \\mathfrak{H}_{\\perp} have zero mean under \\pi_{\\eta}^{X\\mid Y=y} for \\pi_{\\eta}^{Y}-almost every y.",
        "coverage": "NODE_OR_CONTEXT",
        "boundary": "Bounded source prerequisite or B10/B11 statement; no wholepaper claim"
      },
      {
        "id": "A2.SS1.p2",
        "primary": {
          "path": "E:/Samplinglib/runs/20261007-companion-priority/phase-pbps-gamma-preread57/primary-pbps.exactraw.snapshot.html",
          "raw_bytes": 1482128,
          "lf_bytes": 1482128,
          "raw_sha256": "d81e929496ff33f8895ebdb45b5b7f3eba89a069806d97d5bbbd7a6c0c032760",
          "lf_sha256": "d81e929496ff33f8895ebdb45b5b7f3eba89a069806d97d5bbbd7a6c0c032760"
        },
        "byte_range": [
          727706,
          733595
        ],
        "raw_source_snapshot": {
          "path": "E:/Samplinglib/runs/20261007-companion-priority/pbps-real-root-unique62/next-macro-source63/primary-18-A2-SS1-p2.exactraw.snapshot.html",
          "raw_bytes": 5889,
          "lf_bytes": 5889,
          "raw_sha256": "867f37d31c89be99b7218d384e7e1eafec857b4f0da5f51191f6f314828f91c0",
          "lf_sha256": "867f37d31c89be99b7218d384e7e1eafec857b4f0da5f51191f6f314828f91c0"
        },
        "literal_text": "Relative to the decomposition \\mathfrak{H}=\\mathfrak{H}_{\\mathsf{P}}\\oplus\\mathfrak{H}_{\\perp}, we write an operator \\mathsf{T} on \\mathfrak{H} in block form as \\mathsf{T}=\\begin{pmatrix}\\mathsf{T}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}&\\mathsf{T}_{\\mathsf{P}\\perp}\\\\ \\mathsf{T}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}&\\mathsf{T}_{\\perp\\perp}\\end{pmatrix}\\,,\\hskip 20.00003pt\\begin{aligned} \\mathsf{T}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}&\\coloneqq\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{T}\\mathsf{P}\\,,&\\mathsf{T}_{\\mathsf{P}\\perp}&\\coloneqq\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{T}\\mathsf{P}^{\\perp}\\,,\\\\ \\mathsf{T}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}&\\coloneqq\\mathsf{P}^{\\perp}\\mathsf{T}\\mathsf{P}\\,,&\\mathsf{T}_{\\perp\\perp}&\\coloneqq\\mathsf{P}^{\\perp}\\mathsf{T}\\mathsf{P}^{\\perp}\\,.\\end{aligned} (B.3) The first subscript specifies the target subspace and the second the source subspace; thus \\mathsf{T}_{ab}:\\mathfrak{H}_{b}\\to\\mathfrak{H}_{a} for a,b\\in\\{\\mathsf{P},\\perp\\}.",
        "coverage": "NODE_OR_CONTEXT",
        "boundary": "Bounded source prerequisite or B10/B11 statement; no wholepaper claim"
      },
      {
        "id": "A2.SS1.p3",
        "primary": {
          "path": "E:/Samplinglib/runs/20261007-companion-priority/phase-pbps-gamma-preread57/primary-pbps.exactraw.snapshot.html",
          "raw_bytes": 1482128,
          "lf_bytes": 1482128,
          "raw_sha256": "d81e929496ff33f8895ebdb45b5b7f3eba89a069806d97d5bbbd7a6c0c032760",
          "lf_sha256": "d81e929496ff33f8895ebdb45b5b7f3eba89a069806d97d5bbbd7a6c0c032760"
        },
        "byte_range": [
          733596,
          742298
        ],
        "raw_source_snapshot": {
          "path": "E:/Samplinglib/runs/20261007-companion-priority/pbps-real-root-unique62/next-macro-source63/primary-19-A2-SS1-p3.exactraw.snapshot.html",
          "raw_bytes": 8702,
          "lf_bytes": 8702,
          "raw_sha256": "654bd2e3d43cfbb9332da21b4b76c2066f0c7aa4275c5a736d6bb2a6f1552873",
          "lf_sha256": "654bd2e3d43cfbb9332da21b4b76c2066f0c7aa4275c5a736d6bb2a6f1552873"
        },
        "literal_text": "We first apply this block notation to the reflection map \\mathsf{U} from (2.14). We use the same symbol for its pullback on observables: (\\mathsf{U}f)(x,y)\\coloneqq f(\\mathsf{U}(x,y))=f(x,2x-y)\\,. (B.4) This pullback is self-adjoint and unitary, and hence has block matrix \\mathsf{U}=\\begin{pmatrix}\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}&\\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}^{*}\\\\ \\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}&\\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\perp}\\end{pmatrix}\\,. Here \\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}=\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{U}\\mathsf{P} maps \\mathfrak{H}_{\\mathsf{P}} to itself, whereas \\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}=\\mathsf{P}^{\\perp}\\mathsf{U}\\mathsf{P} maps \\mathfrak{H}_{\\mathsf{P}} to \\mathfrak{H}_{\\perp}. Since \\mathsf{U} is self-adjoint and unitary, \\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}} is a self-adjoint contraction on \\mathfrak{H}_{\\mathsf{P}}. Writing \\mathsf{U}^{2}=I in blocks gives \\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}^{*}\\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}=I-\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}^{2}\\,,\\hskip 20.00003pt\\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}^{*}\\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\perp}=-\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}\\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}^{*}\\,. (B.5)",
        "coverage": "NODE_OR_CONTEXT",
        "boundary": "Bounded source prerequisite or B10/B11 statement; no wholepaper claim"
      },
      {
        "id": "A2.E8",
        "primary": {
          "path": "E:/Samplinglib/runs/20261007-companion-priority/phase-pbps-gamma-preread57/primary-pbps.exactraw.snapshot.html",
          "raw_bytes": 1482128,
          "lf_bytes": 1482128,
          "raw_sha256": "d81e929496ff33f8895ebdb45b5b7f3eba89a069806d97d5bbbd7a6c0c032760",
          "lf_sha256": "d81e929496ff33f8895ebdb45b5b7f3eba89a069806d97d5bbbd7a6c0c032760"
        },
        "byte_range": [
          762524,
          764253
        ],
        "raw_source_snapshot": {
          "path": "E:/Samplinglib/runs/20261007-companion-priority/pbps-real-root-unique62/next-macro-source63/primary-20-A2-E8.exactraw.snapshot.html",
          "raw_bytes": 1729,
          "lf_bytes": 1729,
          "raw_sha256": "5a60b7a7667ec1a06d63f370f1711890038e27cb223b63d17031494e7ee0928a",
          "lf_sha256": "5a60b7a7667ec1a06d63f370f1711890038e27cb223b63d17031494e7ee0928a"
        },
        "literal_text": "Y_{+}\\coloneqq X+\\sqrt{\\eta}\\,Z\\,,\\hskip 20.00003ptY_{-}\\coloneqq X-\\sqrt{\\eta}\\,Z\\,,\\hskip 20.00003ptZ\\sim\\mathcal{N}(0,I)\\,,\\hskip 20.00003ptX\\sim\\mu\\,. (B.8)",
        "coverage": "NODE_OR_CONTEXT",
        "boundary": "Bounded source prerequisite or B10/B11 statement; no wholepaper claim"
      },
      {
        "id": "A3.SS1.p2",
        "primary": {
          "path": "E:/Samplinglib/runs/20261007-companion-priority/phase-pbps-gamma-preread57/primary-pbps.exactraw.snapshot.html",
          "raw_bytes": 1482128,
          "lf_bytes": 1482128,
          "raw_sha256": "d81e929496ff33f8895ebdb45b5b7f3eba89a069806d97d5bbbd7a6c0c032760",
          "lf_sha256": "d81e929496ff33f8895ebdb45b5b7f3eba89a069806d97d5bbbd7a6c0c032760"
        },
        "byte_range": [
          1004189,
          1009595
        ],
        "raw_source_snapshot": {
          "path": "E:/Samplinglib/runs/20261007-companion-priority/pbps-real-root-unique62/next-macro-source63/primary-21-A3-SS1-p2.exactraw.snapshot.html",
          "raw_bytes": 5406,
          "lf_bytes": 5406,
          "raw_sha256": "96d3f106bcd0b32f60a5c97b7df3d8f231c571d286884e8ca4aa30cf3b64749b",
          "lf_sha256": "96d3f106bcd0b32f60a5c97b7df3d8f231c571d286884e8ca4aa30cf3b64749b"
        },
        "literal_text": "Recall that the conditional density p_{y} of Y_{-} given Y_{+}=y is p_{y}(u)\\propto\\exp\\Bigl\\{-V((y+u)/2)-\\frac{\\|y-u\\|^{2}}{8\\eta}\\Bigr\\}\\,, and define s_{y}(u)\\coloneqq-\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\nabla V((y+u)/2)-\\frac{y-u}{4\\eta}\\,. Differentiating the normalized conditional density gives \\nabla\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}f(y)=\\mathrm{Cov}\\bigl(f(Y_{-}),s_{y}(Y_{-})\\bigm|Y_{+}=y\\bigr)\\,. (C.1)",
        "coverage": "EXCLUDED",
        "boundary": "Rough gradient analytic route already separate; not needed for B11"
      },
      {
        "id": "A2.Thmtheorem1.p1",
        "primary": {
          "path": "E:/Samplinglib/runs/20261007-companion-priority/phase-pbps-gamma-preread57/primary-pbps.exactraw.snapshot.html",
          "raw_bytes": 1482128,
