        "Construct internal Fact(mY≤m0); Mathlib lpMeas completion and condExpL2=orthogonalProjection give exactHP=ranP, complete macrospace and P acts identity only there. Define A_macro and B_macro with exact types.",
        "Use SAME M(Tu)=PUP(Mu) to show A_macro=e.conjStarAlgEquiv T, preserving actual operator action. Align independent ReflectionL2 U by AE pullback to reuse its fulljoint starB_joint*B_joint=P-A_joint².",
        "Apply generic61 real root existence to SAME scalarD; apply generic62 positive-square uniqueness for canonical scalarΓ. No independent actual62 T witness required and no new real-CFC/finiteL2 premise.",
        "Transport Γ via e.conjStarAlgEquiv. Existing map_mul/map_one/sub plus IsPositive.conj_adjoint and e.adjoint_eq_symm prove positivity and exact typed macro square.",
        "Use subtype.adjoint=orthogonalProjection and adjoint_comp (or inner ext) to restrict the SAME fulljoint Gram: B_macro†∘B_macro=I_HP-A_macro². P∘subtype=subtype and A_joint∘subtype=subtype∘A_macro justify every domain change.",
        "Pull every competing positive macro root back through e.symm; scalar62 uniqueness gives equality. Allmacro norm identity follows exact Gram/root-square energy (not only image witnesses). Genuine original-input Test checks arbitrary f:HP, ΓP/Bmacro norm equality and contractivity incl rank0; optional posterior variance followup55 is not forced into unused direct dependency."
      ],
